Add install script for easy curling (#2)

* add install.sh for easier install method

* linting, dep upgrades that ive been putting off

* use the new install script in the gha

* refine CI, agents, and developer experience

* fix setup action sparse checkout

* isolate setup action checkout

* fold vulnerability scan into lint

* label CI shards and refresh gopherbuzz docs

* serialize console dependency install

* fix CI shard summary label

* order console CI setup before fanout

* build CI magus from checked out revision

* dont check the commit ancestor when dogfooding

* fold project references behind one type and one resolver

* build CI magus from the checked out revision

* let agent install target a directory outside the workspace

* carry a loaded buzz session and its targets as one value through

* reserve a sticky terminal region for failures and a live pool counter

* route every terminal check and escape through the tty package

* fail the build when a _test.go has no source file beside it

* document --embedded, the workspace:// scheme

* regenerate the routing index, graphs, and docs site

* structure CI job logs through a provider contract magus core does

* add GitLab sections; stop printing an inspect hint that cannot work

* require a second Ctrl+C to stop a run

* strip every control sequence in the log viewer, not just colour

* move CI provider syntax out of Go and into spells

* let the host modules do the work a spell was doing by hand

* document the name a caller types, not the one Go declares

* bound and de-fang the CI provider boundary

* document CI providers as an extension point

* correct nested access: backslash qualifies, dot reaches members

* document why a thin ci workflow survives release branches

* qualify namespaces with a backslash across every .buzz source

* reframe the release-branch guidance as common pitfalls

* bound a runaway target with an opt-in deadline

* add tour steps for guardrails and output refs; link the testing guide

* qualify io, ffi, and math namespaces too

* add an Everything here list for the whole branch beneath a page

* register synthesized development pages for navigation, not just search

* show backslash namespace access in the hand-authored docs

* regenerate the docs site, routing indexes, and graphs

* close ten upstream Buzz parity gaps

* support cross-project outputs and reject the shapes that would corrupt

* serve the read-only magus verbs in-process instead of forking

* add vcs tags and cache-yield diagnostics

* reorganise the docs tree into sections and regenerate the site

* fold the remaining unpaired test files; move the es plugin to proto

* close seven more upstream Buzz parity gaps: 27 -> 34 of 83

* close four more parity gaps and gate every one of them with

* add block expressions: from { ... out v; }; 38 -> 40 of 83

* add free identifiers and generic object declarations; 40 -> 42 of 83

* add inline if expressions and catch void; 42 -> 44 of 83

* thread expected types through calls and literals; 44 -> 45 of 83

* fix range precedence and give ranges their methods; 45 -> 47 of 83

* accept an assignment as a void arrow body

* resolve anonymous object literals to their expected object

* gofmt the ext_assert_test import block; it was failing the format gate

* make the agent guard actually fire

* judge file paths from declared outputs

* block repo-wide text search, guard the CWD trap

* teach the escalation ladder and --dry-run instead of

* give targets their args as a list, and key the cache on them

* show forwarded args in --dry-run

* add the magus-buzz skill; skill contract v18

* enforce host agnosticism with a test, and stop printing per-host setup

* make the hook templates real files

* colocate the hook templates with the guide

* record what host parity actually is, verified and not

* give Codex the guard, using the generic templates unchanged

* rewrite the OpenCode plugin against a real OpenCode, not the spec

* make the templates a linted project

* teach instead of prevent, and let a project declare its own name
