-- e5b587512d361c62a43075badd7724e7ada5c1e3 --
restrict the glossary term click-to-reveal to touch devices: the reveal and the hover popover render the exact same cardBody() content, so on a hover-capable device the popover already covers everything a click would show, making a redundant split-open just for clicking a term that already peeked open on hover; let those clicks follow the link normally and keep the reveal for touch, where hover never fires and click is the only way to see the definition

-- 8ec53b68fb47f8c1368f0c6ff68aec0b8133f6d3 --
soften the glossary split-reveal's inset shadow: the previous pass deepened it to compensate for a since-removed duplicate, but on its own that landed too dark and heavy; pull the alpha and blur back down for a subtler recess

-- 9aff2edab0b718a9d5260093492b52021ceba722 --
gate the glossary term hover popover on matchMedia(hover: hover): a touch tap fires a synthetic mouseenter/focus just before its click as part of the browser's tap-compatibility sequence, so tapping a term flashed the hover popover open right alongside the split-reveal it was actually meant to trigger; hover-capable devices (including keyboard nav on a desktop, which reports hover:hover) are unaffected

-- b848190e8ce7bb94b36110e049a7c8ddc6bfc6ac --
