-- 2f02f9d747507eb280fce3393074953ffb06d433 --
magus.needs takes target functions only: same-project exports by reference (forward refs work, bodies run post-load) and cross-project import members as real callables (alias.target() dispatches directly); add magus.needsGlob as the separate pattern verb; remove the magus.target namespace (literal/glob/regex/expand_globs), the Buzz TargetQuery mirror, and types.TargetQuery; resolve identifier and needsGlob edges in the static extractor and dry tracer so the graph is unchanged and dependency typos fail at load; export gopherbuzz vm.Value.Equal (Buzz == semantics) for host-side function identity; migrate all magusfiles (proto gains a conventional generate target wrapping buf-generate), docs, tour, starter, examples, and tests

-- 7a6df37001da87fbc6b16afd8a98551a0211e0c1 --
fingerprint dev builds for daemon adoption instead of matching on unknown; gate background jobs the same way; resolve adopted runs from the client cwd not the daemon getwd; fail loudly when zero targets resolve; journal the client cwd

-- 9a0e8b5acb450a89cd5ca6199ea0a38f1ed432c1 --
fix a cross-build list.indexOf divergence in gopherbuzz: the element compare used Value.RawEqual (raw tag+num bits), which is heap reference identity only in the nanbox build; under buzz_safe/buzz_unsafe num is 0 for every heap value so any same-tag heap needle matched the first element (["a","b"].indexOf("z") returned 0); export valuesEqual as Value.Equal (Buzz == semantics, validated against the upstream buzz binary: string content, list/map/object/function reference identity, null on no match) and use it in indexOf; correct the false pointer-identity claims in the RawEqual doc comment and bytecode_test.go, and harden TestSlotEnvEquivalence to Equal; add cross-build conformance tests (TestListIndexOfConformance, TestValueEqual) green under all three value-representation tags

-- 7c97d6496df5cd231d97ca6999bc79b30be0424f --
add knowledge.vcs.authorship toggle (default on) to include or omit the author node/edge layer

The @vcs shard's author nodes and authored edges are useful context but not always wanted; gate them behind a *bool config (nil = on, mirroring hints.enabled) so a run can keep only the per-file vcs_* attrs. Thread VCSAuthorship through Inputs and assembleVCS (skip author collection when off), fold the flag into vcsInputFingerprint so toggling invalidates the cached shard, regenerate the env binding (MAGUS_KNOWLEDGE_VCS_AUTHORSHIP), and refresh docs/knowledge.md (also drops the stale vcs-inputs.json reference and now documents the author layer)

-- 1deda1d357cce5c3355d95f7e0254f1ebb8dc7bb --
drop the arbitrary per-author fan-out cap on `authored` edges: the max_commits history window already bounds the scan, so the edges are proportional to recent activity, not the whole repo - a dominant/solo maintainer legitimately authoring many files is a fact to teach the agent, not a god-node smell to summarize away, and any query stays bounded by its neighborhood budget; no config knob (the existing window is the bound). Give @vcs its own vcsAssemblyVersion in the input fingerprint so an assembly-shape change invalidates just that shard on an unchanged HEAD, instead of leaning on a global schema bump (addresses a review finding)

-- faf9a6c32f40728ee599057a05c368c46b439799 --
fix a phantom-node bug in the @vcs input-fingerprint cache found by an adversarial review: the cached shard filters onto the LIVE file nodes, which move when the working tree changes without a commit (a tracked source file deleted-but-uncommitted is no longer a node), so a HEAD-only fingerprint could reuse a shard referencing files assembleBuzz no longer emits, leaving phantom file nodes + authored edges until the next commit; fold the uncommitted-file set (VCSDriver.DirtyFiles) into the fingerprint so any tracked add/delete re-scans and re-filters, while a content edit to an already-dirty file still reuses the shard (committed history is unchanged)

-- 09dc8b24d878fe517f3cd10dffe0d0af76fa4147 --
add author nodes + authored edges to the knowledge graph (schema v6): mint an `author` node per git contributor with an `authored` edge to each node-backed file they touched, so `explain author:<name>` shows what they maintain and a file's emergent authors sit against its declared CODEOWNERS owner; a per-author fan-out cap (maxAuthorFanout) gives a prolific maintainer a files_authored count instead of a god node's worth of edges, and the edges stay path-based (no project dependency) so they ride the @vcs input-fingerprint cache; extracted facts only, aggregate author analytics stay in insight

-- df92b8244d1e6ce05b063ba5016650943d495c3a --
cache the knowledge graph's git-history scan through the standard shard store instead of a bespoke vcs-inputs.json sidecar: shardMeta gains an input fingerprint (HEAD + window + schema, SHA256 like everything else) recorded in the manifest; the composition root skips the expensive ChangesByCommit scan when that fingerprint is unchanged and Sync reuses the @vcs shard from disk (a retention pass loads a skipped-but-fresh input-fingerprinted shard rather than pruning it), so an unchanged tree pays no scan and no extra serialization; delete vcsInputCache/readVCSCache/writeVCSCache; the max_commits window (default 1000) bounds the scan so it never walks a whole monorepo's history

-- 8c3680cf7f4a3f33f041a30045e92051836eb727 --
document the completed console CSS naming + PF-swap pass in PATTERNFLY.md: the ~323-class rename is done area-by-area, every authored class conforms to the console-<area> formula (acceptance sweep returns nothing), and PF-first swaps replaced the segmented switch (ToggleGroup), filter/charm/badge chips (Labels) with premade components

-- 4f6ce8c4b08bedb974c43f982a47e577efeed70c --
console CSS naming pass (activity area): drop the activity surface's three unstyled vestigial classes (activity-app, activity-conn, the bare name label) so the trail is pure console-render-* + PF, and fix a pre-existing dead .graph-empty-state class selector in the shell cold-state rule to the actual #graph-empty-state id; the console now carries no bare, ad-hoc, or unprefixed authored class names

-- 1e6725f5ef3b508b3fbab65f908822d77a20b0fc --
console CSS naming pass (dashboard area): swap the charm effect pills and header count chips for PF Labels, rename the shared glossary link to console-render-glosslink, and rename all remaining dashboard tile chrome (attention hero, stat strips, pool grid, gantt, utilization heatmap, charts, dense tables, config/service/metric/insight tiles) to the console-dashboard-* formula; move pool/gantt/hero/table state onto data-* attributes; leave the vendored uPlot classes untouched

-- ab565df63fa845da7c60afd67659bf0c73c61a4f --
console CSS naming pass (graph area): swap the live/snapshot badges for PF Labels and rename all remaining graph-explorer chrome (sidebar node cloud, legend, explain card, Ask views, color groups, term-prompt controls, reference disclosures) to the console-graph-* formula; move kind coloring to data-kind and every active/open/disabled/error state onto data-* attributes; update the shell console.css graph refs in lockstep

-- 067806a1e7f9ecb344a003a38dfeab05886caf7d --
console CSS naming pass (log area): swap the custom sliding segmented switch for a PF ToggleGroup and the parsed-filter chips for PF Labels (deleting their custom CSS), and rename the genuinely component-less log chrome (trace waterfall, zoom control, filter row, ref-identity pills, help disclosures) to the console-log-* formula; move view/waterfall/highlight/filter state onto data-* attributes and delete the dead Pico file-bar frame

-- 1d13d1113051c69ea552fdf3c0ab5f9e93f6a238 --
console CSS naming pass (shell area): delete the dead Pico app-bar/waffle-launcher block, move the body app/fill modes to data-console-app/data-console-fill, and rename the surviving shell chrome (status bar right cluster + items, floating theme-cycle button, refresh toast) to the console-shell-* formula; drop the inert container-fluid/console-statusbar class hooks in favor of the #console-statusbar id

-- 4bfa23b03cfad90616955403fc6ff2171d413b28 --
console CSS naming pass (render area): rename the shared log/activity render model to the console-render-* formula; sections/badges/ANSI spans/lines/frame + the shared toolbar button parts become console-render-<block>__<element>--<modifier>, transient state (collapse/status accent/highlight/drag) moves to data-* attributes, and no bare ad-hoc class names remain in the render layer

-- 8f1ad0d2d528a0c81ff58dbeb2381076351b6e75 --
fold the last commit's author onto file nodes as vcs_last_author, so a file's emergent maintainer (who actually edits it) sits next to its declared CODEOWNERS owner - the owner-of-record vs who is really editing, a gap a pure code-graph cannot see; capture it in aggregateFileHistory from the commit history already scanned (near-free), and version the vcs-inputs cache so a warm cache repopulates with the new field

-- 3988fe943a9d080e05d7c3ef8b69fcadf3b325b9 --
index the build I/O layer and authored markdown in the knowledge graph (schema v5): turn each target's declared magus.outputs/inputs into produces/consumes edges to the file and doc nodes they match, so a generated file is self-labeled by its producing target and a target walks to exactly what it writes (a per-glob fan-out cap keeps a broad declaration from making a god node); broaden doc ingestion workspace-wide - descending meaningful dot-dirs (.claude/skills for SKILL.md, .github) and skipping only true noise and nested worktrees - tag every authored markdown with a role attr from a universal filename convention (readme/agent/skill/changelog/contributing/license), and attach each doc to its project via contains; make role a queryable field so `kind:doc role:agent` finds the agent files in any repo

-- f848542ed2a95505c2a9fc46a5e5ad297f21e5c5 --
replace em-dashes with hyphens in the user-facing doc-strings the doc generators render (std module Doc fields, the go/buzz spell op docs, internal/manpage Long descriptions, and the magus-docs/manpage intro strings) and regenerate docs/{buzz/modules,spells,manpage}; the rendered reference pages are now plain ASCII, matching the convention for user-facing strings

-- dbe1d1fe2f4500d2dbd021b4374f41c7fc1c08e9 --
replace em-dashes with hyphens and the ellipsis character with ... across the hand-written documentation prose (charms, telemetry, remote-cache, and the diagnostic-code pages); plain-ASCII punctuation reads cleaner and matches the repo's user-facing-string convention

-- f1a0709330b3da935e0b763359c35a99d89900d1 --
give the docs plain page titles: drop the "Anatomy of a magus X" framing (charms, targets, spells, workspace) and the descriptive H1 subtitles (cache, sandbox, engines, mcp, operations) so each page's H1 is just its basic technical name, matching its frontmatter title

-- c63bae550f845106ea34b427fd7690f2324b7c62 --
add magus-examples: capture real `magus explain`/`path` output from a curated fixture graph and inject it into docs/knowledge.md between <!-- example:<slug> --> markers, so the worked examples in the docs are the actual rendered output (never hand-typed) and cannot drift; wire it into the docs content-generate target (knowledge.md output + render/knowledge/magus-examples inputs) so the existing generate + vcs.isDirty gate keeps them current; singularize '1 node reaches this' in the explain card

-- dbdad48056ec4b1635dfea5394c5b8873c3fd79f --
render `magus explain` and `magus path` as compact natural-language text by default (CLI and MCP): fold each edge's direction into a verb (used by / depends on / part of / required by), group by relation with a count before multi-item lists, and list full node IDs (the token for the next call) - replacing the <--uses-- adjacency notation that made the reader invert the arrow and the ~4x-larger JSON the MCP tools returned; the shared renderer lives in internal/render so CLI and MCP emit identically, and -o json stays the structured opt-in for agents that parse

-- 3fcd3b4acc9677e96ac8ea3a7f6d0688e22e40a5 --
retire the knowledge-graph command kind and move the model onto the op (schema v4): a command node's rendered argv was always identical to its op's static base command, so it was a redundant per-target copy of the op; an op now carries an `argv` attr and `uses` the `tool` (argv[0]) it runs, so `explain tool:go` lists every op that runs go, `kind:tool` is the workspace's toolchain inventory, and a target reaches its tool via the existing target->op edge (no synthetic targets, no dry tracer, nothing added to the wasm closure); refine the orphan lens to flag only a spell the workspace declares AND that provides ops AND that nothing runs, so an available-but-undeclared builtin and a structural no-op spell are no longer false positives; teach magus-architecture to audit the domain model with the graph

-- 8ed49938d38c69e6e34e29467f319b39ea55ee40 --
document the STRICT custom-CSS naming methodology for the console (PATTERNFLY.md): every class we author (the escape-hatch bits PatternFly has no component for) follows console-<area>-<block>__<element>--<modifier> - a namespaced, BEM-structured formula mirroring pf-v6-*, with a closed area set (shell/dashboard/log/graph/activity/render), state carried on data-* not modifier classes, and NO bare/ad-hoc class names. Includes the legacy->convention example map and flags the pending ~323-class rename pass as a dedicated area-by-area follow-up

-- ee9d46bd612cc2ded14f111e813967ac94208eae --
PatternFly migration W4 (cutover): remove Pico entirely - the console now runs on PatternFly alone

W0-W3 kept Pico loaded alongside PatternFly so the mid-migration console stayed coherent; W4 removes it. Repointed every remaining --pico-*/--c-* reference in the kept sheets to PF/--console- tokens: deleted console.css's dead --c-hit/--c-ok/--c-err/--c-info/--c-miss/--c-warn palette (the surfaces read --console-* now; the one live --c-info in ::selection -> --console-accent), dropped the Pico font-family plumbing (PF base + tokens.css supply the system stacks), and repointed the ~35 shell rules (title bar, status frame, launcher, tiling divider/focus, disabled-button contrast, help glyph). DELETED the four Pico-era sheets - src/assets/pico.min.css + src/styles/{site,theme,ui-panels}.css - and pulled their <link>s from index.html, their esbuild lines from package.json's build-css, and their entries from sw.js precache (the theme SCRIPT src/theme.ts / theme.js is untouched). Migrated the live dependents a scan of JS-injected class names surfaced: the log filter chips (.qchip, built by filter.ts) into logs.css, the refresh toast (.sw-toast, injected by refresh-toast.ts) into overrides.css with a PF-token button style now that Pico's button base is gone, and the .ref-section hide (previously in ui-panels.css - the ref-drawer is unused in the decoupled console) into overrides.css. Bumped sw.js BUILD_ID to w4-patternfly so clients drop the old cache; updated PATTERNFLY.md.

Verified: grep for --pico-/--c-hit/etc across src returns NOTHING; typecheck 0, 70 tests pass, build clean (no CSS warnings); gen/ ships no pico/site/ui-panels/theme.css (reclaimed ~132KB raw, 1720->1588KB); index.html links only patternfly/tokens/console/overrides. Browser-verified on PF-ALONE (fresh port, Pico tokens resolve to empty, PF tokens resolve, no console errors): all four surfaces + Home mount, and the dashboard demo (attention hero, live activity, pool grid, cache stat tiles + their accent colors) renders correctly in BOTH light and dark. The PatternFly migration W0-W4 is complete - the console is fully on PatternFly. Remaining follow-up: PurgeCSS over the ~683KB PF base (the deferred precache optimization noted in PATTERNFLY.md), plus a dead .console-bar/.site-header block in console.css that never renders in the decoupled console (a clean prune).

-- 563e1d1d8f4a2208f697b2b9f8a3b0d436c4b45a --
PatternFly migration W3 (activity surface): migrate the activity trail chrome to PatternFly

The activity surface builds its DOM in TS (no own CSS - it reuses the log viewer's classes). W3-logs kept the shared .panel/.log-scroll/.log-body/buildSection frame + entry rendering alive and token-repointed, so the trail ENTRIES were already PF-native in color; this migrates activity's TS-built CHROME to match the log viewer's PF surface. buildScaffold now emits a PF Toolbar (title left, connection note + Refresh right), a PF secondary Button for Refresh + the demo button, and a PF EmptyState for the cold "No daemon connected" state - dropping the old Pico .file-bar/.log-actions/.btn-group/.outline/.console-empty-* markup (the latter now used by nothing, so it can go at the W4 cutover). The empty state carries the log-empty class alongside pf-v6-c-empty-state purely for logs.css's `.log-empty[hidden] { display: none }` toggle (PF EmptyState is display:flex, which would otherwise beat the hidden attribute the render loop sets). adapter.ts/adapter.test.ts and render/sections.ts are untouched (the pure tested boundary). Done directly (not via a sub-agent - the delegated attempt returned an anomalous non-response and made no changes). typecheck 0, 70 tests pass, build clean (no CSS warnings); browser-verified: PF toolbar + Refresh button, the PF EmptyState cold state hides correctly on demo, and the 14-entry demo trail renders with its status accents. All four W3 surfaces (dashboard/logs/graph/activity) are now on PatternFly.

-- 51c43e4a5ceaa3847c23bb9ba782ec7e7aa9305b --
PatternFly migration W3 (graph explorer surface): migrate the graph chrome to PatternFly

Per the plan the d3 force-graph STAGE (canvas/SVG nodes+edges, force sim, drag/zoom, mermaid path) stays custom - only its CHROME migrates and its color reads repoint. The stage toolbar (fit/open-file/copy-mermaid/fullscreen), the legend toggle, and the layout toggle become PF Buttons (secondary, small, icon+text) keeping their IDs + .btn-icon/.btn-label hooks; the cold "Nothing loaded yet" state becomes a PF EmptyState mirroring logs/dashboard (with a proper bordered secondary demo button, dodging the role=button/Pico white-fill trap). The sidebar magus-query prompt, node cloud, reference details, legend, explain card, and live/snapshot badges stay bespoke/ID-scoped (a left sidebar + details, not a horizontal PF Toolbar - same call logs made for its segmented control), colors repointed. explorer.js is unchanged except comment/token-string edits.

Node-kind colors (the silent-regression surface): a 14-kind categorical palette in tokens.css mapped onto PF's nonstatus data-viz families, with semantically-adjacent pairs at lighter --200 sibling shades so a shade confusion never crosses a boundary. Fixed a real PF-v6 gotcha: the plain nonstatus tokens are NOT theme-aware (light values in both themes), so added a :root.pf-v6-theme-dark override block sourcing the global dark data-viz values - verified 14 distinct colors in light AND 14 distinct in dark via getComputedStyle. All --pico-*/--syntax-panel-bg reads across graph.css + main.ts repointed to --pf-t--*/--console-*; graph.css's two per-theme --gk-* palette blocks collapse to one alias block. Fixed a stray */ in a graph.css comment (--pico-*/--c-* closed the comment early). typecheck 0, 70 tests pass, build green (no CSS warnings); browser-verified the PF EmptyState cold state + PF toolbar buttons in light.

NOTE (pre-existing, orthogonal): the graph demo fetches ./graph.json (main.ts:273) but the standalone console has no committed demo graph.json - the decouple never carried the website's demo graph into the console build, so the graph demo cannot render until that data is wired into gen/graph/. Flagged separately; not a migration regression.

-- 06b114da0bf351a34272c3fb61f6116424ebd1bb --
PatternFly migration W3 (log viewer surface): migrate the log viewer chrome to PatternFly

CSS/scaffold/tokens only - log-viewer.js is BYTE-IDENTICAL to before (zero JS changes), so every ID/data-* contract and exported signature is preserved and there is no behavioral risk. The file/query bar becomes a PF Toolbar (filter + action groups) with PF FormControl inputs and PF Buttons (Pause/Collapse/Copy/Copy command/Share/Open in graph/Fullscreen); the cold "Nothing loaded yet" state becomes a PF EmptyState mirroring the dashboard. The custom-rendered pieces PatternFly has no component for stay as the escape hatch with colors repointed to PF-native --console-* tokens: the ANSI-colored log body + collapsible sections, the trace waterfall, and the Pretty|Raw / Log|Timeline sliders (a single aria-pressed <button> the viewer JS toggles, deeply wired - the one place that fought PF's discrete ToggleGroup, kept as the sliding control). Added 6 ANSI color slots to tokens.css (red/green/yellow reuse the status palette so a red line matches a [fail] badge; blue/magenta/cyan map to PF nonstatus tokens) - caught + fixed a real regression where ANSI blue first mapped to PF's info token, which is a purple-blue that collided with magenta; repointed to true blue so all six terminal hues are provably distinct. logs.css sheds its Pico-era toolbar/filter/docs-page rules (417->366 lines); added the PF Toolbar sheet. The shared classes activity reuses (.panel/.file-bar/.log-*/buildSection) are kept alive (colors-only repoint) so activity is unchanged. typecheck 0, 70 tests pass (query.test.ts green - pure logic untouched), build green; browser-verified the toolbar + PF EmptyState cold state in light, ANSI body colors distinct in light + dark.

-- a8747b8538fdcfdd3893c12524345c191aa4016a --
PatternFly migration W3 (dashboard surface): migrate the dashboard to PatternFly

Leverage the shared card.ts tile factory - migrated ONCE to a pf-v6-c-card (header/toggle/title/actions/body) - so ~17 tiles (pool, cache*, latency, remote, targets, mcp, buzz, sandbox, activity, workspaces, services, config, gantt, the 5 insight lens tiles, ...) get PF styling from one edit; collapse is a data-collapsed attribute + a bare caret button (PF's expandable-card toggle needs a pficon webfont the console does not ship). Bespoke pieces: the attention hero (always-visible section), utilization (already W0). The connect/empty screen is rebuilt in scaffold.html as a PF EmptyState + a PF Gallery of app cards + PF FormControl/Buttons, all dash-* app-hook IDs preserved.

Charts (silent-regression surface): uplot.ts + the chart tiles read CSS custom properties at runtime, so repoint every read from the old --c-* palette to the PF-native, theme-aware --console-* tokens (added --console-status-danger, --console-chart-axis, --console-chart-grid, --console-accent-hover to tokens.css - all mapped to --pf-t-* so they resolve correctly in light AND dark with no per-theme code). Verified the resolved values are distinct in both themes: latency p50=running / p95=warn / p99=danger are three distinct hues; cache hit-rate=ok green; axis/grid grays invert for dark. Two locked-token-map consequences (flagged, not bugs): running renders PURPLE (PF info token is blue-purple, not Pico blue) consistently across pool/gantt/hero/links; queued and failed both land on PF danger red (queued kept at 0.55 opacity to distinguish).

data/streaming logic (state.ts/transport.ts/demo.ts) untouched; dashboard.css sheds its .tile*/.hub-*/.dash-connect-* Pico blocks (454->411 lines), added EmptyState to patternfly.css. Real <button>/PF-button markup avoids the W2 role=button/Pico white-fill trap. typecheck 0, 70 tests pass, build green; browser-verified demo mode in light + dark: cards, hero, pool/utilization grids, cache stat tiles, connect EmptyState, and the chart token resolution.

-- 66402393da976fc06cecf1bde5d78b241d14614e --
PatternFly migration W1+W2: finalize the foundation and rebuild the console SHELL chrome on PatternFly

W1 (foundation) was substantially delivered by the W0 spike - PF base loaded, a fresh tokens.css, and a theme.ts that syncs both pf-v6-theme-dark and Pico's data-theme with pre-paint no-flash + a matchMedia auto-follow; verified a fresh OS-dark load applies the class and the auto/light/dark cycle sets both. (The W0 "auto-follow gap" was a test-harness artifact - the pane's post-load colorScheme switch does not fire a real matchMedia change; a fresh load honors it.) Pico base stays loaded until the W4 cutover so the still-Pico surfaces keep working.

W2 (shell) rebuilds the rest of the chrome on PatternFly, building on W0's tab strip: the bottom status bar chips become PF Labels (the frame + liveness dot are the audited escape hatch in a new small src/styles/overrides.css, colored from --console-* tokens); the floating gear is a PF control Button and its settings popover a PF Menu + Form/FormControl; the home launcher is a PF Gallery of Cards; the command palette and keybindings overlay are PF ModalBox-in-Backdrop; the tiling divider/focus-ring/in-pane launcher repoint to PF tokens. Every ID/role/data-* contract that console.js/main.ts/palette.ts/keybindings.ts/console-settings.js mounts into is kept, and the pure logic (matchCommands, keybindingRows) + their unit tests are untouched. console.css shrinks 48% (17KB -> 8.8KB) as its Pico-era status-bar/fab/launcher/palette/keybindings blocks are deleted; the needed PF component sheets (Label, Menu, Form, FormControl, ModalBox, Backdrop, Bullseye) are added to patternfly.css. Fixed a role=button trap (Pico, still loaded, styles [role=button] as a primary button -> white-on-white cards) and a stray */ in an overrides.css comment.

Net bundle: +11.6KB gzipped vs W0 (added component sheets, minus deleted console.css) - PurgeCSS remains the W4 follow-up. typecheck 0, 70 tests pass, build green; browser-verified in light AND dark: home launcher, gear + settings popover, mod+k palette, keybindings overlay, split-pane divider/focus.

-- 6abb0944922d177adac377d31356cc9b2252d556 --
