-- 40867b28aeae537f8e3e807343175138f173cc64 --
make the generated docs-markdown story cohesive: de-collide the manpage "gen" dirs, move docs-content generation into the docs project, and give the manpage roff/md an owned split

The docs manpages lived in docs/manpage/gen/ - a "gen" dir nested in the content tree that collided with the SSG's own docs/gen/ output, forcing the renderer to strip a phantom "gen" URL segment in two places and the walk skip-set to carry a special carve-out. Rename docs/manpage/gen/*.md -> docs/manpage/*.md and manpage/gen/*.1 -> manpage/*.1 (roff); because the render already stripped "gen" from manpage URLs, the public URLs (/manpage/<cmd>/) are byte-identical, so no urls.lock or redirect churn - and the "gen"-stripping hacks in render_url (cleanURL), render_html (cleanTarget), and the render.buzz breadcrumb are deleted, plus the skip-set carve-out comment simplified.

Move ownership of the derived docs markdown (Buzz module reference, spell docs, CLI manpage md) from the ROOT magusfile's docs_generate INTO the docs project: a new docs content-generate target runs cmd/magus-{docs,spelldocs,manpage} from the docs cwd and drift-gates its own outputs, with the generators' Go sources added to the docs project's sources so a change to std/host/spells still marks docs affected. The root no longer generates docs content. Unify the manpage story as an owned split: docs owns the markdown manpages (site content), the root owns the roff manpages (a distribution artifact for man), both serialized from the same internal/manpage registry via cmd/magus-manpage, cross-referenced. Sync docs/buzz/modules/http.md to the reworked http.server options API (regenerated; TestModuleDocsUpToDate green). Update cmd/magus-manpage + magus-spelldocs defaults/hints, targetgraph.go comments, and the manpage links in README + docs prose.

Verified: go build + std/render/manpage/magus-docs tests + gofmt clean; render in-file tests 41 pass; a scratch render emits every manpage page at its unchanged /manpage/<cmd>/ URL (19/19, no manpage/gen leak); regen reproduces docs/manpage/*.md byte-identically. NOTE root MAGUS.md + docs/MAGUS.md are pre-existingly stale (predate the console-decouple merge) and refresh on main under generate:rw.

-- 0cdc9bad353430f5dab5a388c64ddb184428d4d6 --
add a Shared Service dev loop that serves both gen trees, and give http.server a validated options object

The console decouple left two committed sites (docs/gen at the root, console/gen at /console/ per the Pages assembly), so front them with ONE local server. Rework http.server to take a single options-map bag instead of positional (dir, port) - the host-binding boundary has no struct tag, so a validated map[string]any IS the forward-compatible options object (add a future spa/headers/tls key with no signature break): {dir} for a single root XOR {mounts} for a prefix->dir map (longest-prefix wins, so /console/ shadows the docs render's /console/ redirect stub), plus {port}; unknown keys, missing/both dir+mounts, and bad value types all error loudly in plain ASCII rather than silently defaulting. Drop the intermediate http.mounts; regenerate host/gen; migrate the docs serve + example callers. Add the canonical root serve target: a full dev loop that serves both via the mount options AND hot-rebuilds on source change - a docs markdown edit re-renders docs/gen through a new fast docs render target (render.site_render only, no drift-gated generate), a console src edit rebuilds console/gen via pnpm; watches sources only (gen and node_modules are in IgnoreDirs) so a rebuild never retriggers the watch. Remove the now-subsumed docs-only serve. Verified: go build + std tests + gofmt clean; host/gen regenerates idempotently; the validation errors, the docs-root / SPA-at-/console/ routing (200/200/404, correct titles), and both hot-rebuild mechanisms all reproduce.

