-- 7d6038f100fed7f0e46c202c0dac49047d357867 --
add the Activity surface - the fourth and final core console lens: the daemon's audit trail (magus.activity.v1) painted with the SAME foldable, status-accented sections as the log viewer via the tested activityToModel adapter + shared buildSection, so a run's output and the trail read as one design; it has no standalone page, so it is a new page-less surface kind - a moduleSurface() factory (sibling to standaloneSurface) that dynamically imports a bundle by URL and calls its activate(host) which builds its own scaffold, keeping the console frame lazy (activity is a separate ~190kb bundle loaded only when opened, console.js stays ~6kb); it lists a page via ActivityService.ListActivity when a daemon is reachable (a #live link or the last daemon the dashboard remembered) and renders a synthesized demo trail on #demo so the design is inspectable offline; drop the now-unused stubPage + its CSS (all four surfaces are real); verified demo trail (7 ok/error-accented foldable sections), cold empty state, see-the-demo, and fold in the harness

-- e601fb19a8517e0a3453166f62af7a598aad0e8f --
wire the graph explorer as a real console surface: register it through standaloneSurface and make it console-mountable - defer the canvas/context + DOM handles behind a resolveDom() called from an exported activate() (they were captured at import, so the console importing the bundle before injecting the scaffold threw on canvas.getContext), guard the auto-boot on #graph-canvas, and fetch the demo graph.json relative to the bundle (import.meta.url) not the document so it resolves when mounted at the console's path; add a console.css full-height flex chain for a surface mounted in a tab pane (#console-outlet > div[data-tab-id] > main > .graph-app/.panel) - the standalone full-bleed rules key on the page's single <main> and do not reach the deeper console nesting, so the canvas and the cold empty state were collapsing to zero height; verified cold empty state centers and the demo graph (1648 nodes) renders, logs and dashboard still fill correctly

-- 3c49215ab5e8b479425f2abcb256a23b45d92fa4 --
wire the dashboard as a real console surface and DRY the surface wrapper into a shared factory: standaloneSurface(console/standalone.ts) lifts an app's <main> from its built page, ensures its css, imports the prebuilt esm bundle by URL, and boots it via activate() - logs and dashboard now register through it (deletes the bespoke logs/surface.ts); make the dashboard boot-deferrable like the log viewer (rename boot->exported activate, auto-boot only when #dash-connect is present at import) AND guard its self-wired shell chrome (initNav/initSearch/initRefDrawer/initConsoleSettings) behind the same signal, so mounting it in the console no longer injects a duplicate nav/search into the outlet; standalone dashboard verified unchanged (chrome + demo tiles), embedded verified clean (no orphan panes, demo reveals, switch preserves state, close tears down)

