make the console frame class-free: drive the tab strip, launcher, and panes off ids + role/aria/data selectors instead of custom classes, matching Pico's semantic-HTML expectation; tabs are #console-tabs [role=tab] with [aria-selected]/[data-close]/[data-new], the launcher is #console-outlet [data-surface=home] with [data-open] cards, a pane is #console-outlet > div[data-tab-id], stubs are [data-surface=stub]; no visual change, verified the frame opens/switches/renders

-- 956d1d0658d84b87c71d2e36c46ef5c8c56c676c --
add docs/dependencies.md: the needs vs depends_on model, end to end

The dependency story was scattered across getting-started (needs),
workspace.md (depends_on), and affected.md (the edges the closure walks),
with nothing tying them together. New page: the decision rule between the
two mechanisms, the cross-project needs-into-depends_on fold and its
literal-only discipline, what a bare depends_on does NOT do, the caching
interplay (a cache hit means needs children never dispatch; needs children
aren't independently cached; the coarse project-wide key is the safety
margin), the both-arms static-graph-vs-dry-run rule, cycle/error messages,
glob/regex needs scoping (glob("build") is suffix shorthand, not exact
match), and services reached via needs.

