-- 0efda157f439f839e2b655e78ded17c5db3b3e69 --
services.md: add a caching note

services.md never mentioned caching at all. Add one paragraph: a service
op's target is inherently uncached (servesTarget forces NoCache regardless
of skip_cache), not an author opt-in - caching a service would mean replaying
a stale "success" without ever starting the process. Cross-links spells.md's
existing op-kind explanation and cache.md's control list.

-- cd9653046899bbb28a7b41f587d862dc4d28fcb3 --
cache.md: name the skip/bust controls; add the granularity note

cache.md described no-cache conceptually but never named the four
user-facing controls together: skip_cache policy, --no-cache flag,
magus.bust_cache, magus clean --cache, and cache.immutable each got no
mention or a scattered one-off paragraph. Consolidate into one
"Opting out and busting" table with each control's scope and semantics.

Add the granularity note this was missing: baseStep seeds every target's
Step.Sources with the union of every bound spell's needs plus the magusfile,
so a project binding go and docker has magus run build keying on Dockerfile
changes too - deliberately coarse (a safety margin, not a bug), but worth
naming since it means same-project targets invalidate together more than
their names suggest.

