-- f0f04e17ce141055484f5187442cff89ae904c94 --
harden selfupdate against wrong-length pubkeys, out-of-order/malformed index entries, unversioned dev-build auto-select, and index/manifest version mismatch; drop unread index fields; rename FindAssetsFromIndex to FindAssets

-- 9f37c4d39a58c9ec23f61695aeae44cd3c63eeef --
rewrite magus self update to read only the site index.json; delete the GitHub API path

Discovery now reads gen/public/release/index.json exclusively. The GitHub
API client (apiBase()/FetchRelease) is deleted with it, removing the
unauthenticated 60 req/hr rate limit that blocked CI.

index.json.sig is verified with Ed25519 against the pinned release key
before any data is trusted. Artifact integrity is still anchored by the
signed SHA256SUMS chain.

Downgrade/freeze protection: moving to a lower semver than the running
binary is refused unless the user passes an explicit --version (still
requires --force) or --force alone. Auto-latest silently downgrading
is never allowed.

Discovery URL is overridable via Options.DiscoveryURL or MAGUS_UPDATE_URL
env var, giving organisations that self-host the site a private update
channel for free; documented in MAGUS_UPDATE_URL entry in EnvVarDocs.

New types: ReleaseIndex, IndexRelease, IndexArtifact; new functions:
FetchAndVerifyIndex, SelectRelease, FindAssetsFromIndex. Old: GitHubRelease,
FetchRelease, FindAssets (renamed), apiBase() all deleted.

Options.APIBase renamed to Options.DiscoveryURL; cmd layer override var
renamed overrideAPIBase -> overrideDiscoveryURL.

Tests: whole-struct require.Equal on parsed index/manifest; downgrade
refusal from index; discovery URL override (Options.DiscoveryURL);
MAGUS_UPDATE_URL env override; bad sig -> refuse; unreachable -> stop
with clear error; yanked release skipped; explicit-version downgrade
still requires --force. Coverage raised from ~72% to ~80% (package),
~84% (combined).

